   "daf": "95a",
   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ הַתּוֹלֵשׁ מֵעָצִיץ נָקוּב — חַיָּיב, וְשֶׁאֵינוֹ נָקוּב — פָּטוּר. וְרַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן פּוֹטֵר בָּזֶה וּבָזֶה.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» «One who severs» a leaf or a fruit «from» a plant growing in «a perforated flowerpot» on Shabbat «is liable,» as a plant in a flowerpot with holes in it has the legal status of a plant connected to the ground. Picking from it is prohibited due to reaping. «And» one who picks from an «imperforated» pot «is exempt,» but it is prohibited to do so ab initio. «And Rabbi Shimon deems» one who does so «exempt in» both «this,» the case of the perforated flowerpot, «and that,» the case of the imperforated flowerpot."
  }
 ],
